    "markdown": "- [![Valid](https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/org-theme-wordmark/619465f9-42b1-4ed6-a742-c0093be332f3/c2e32b0e-a20c-4833-86f7-5e980d568641/4d49034a-2f73-4359-908f-8e40d4a26b33.png)](https://valid.co/)\n- [Back to Valid’s Job Listings](https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/Valid)\n\n# App, Performance Marketing Analyst\n\n## Location\n\nRemote or SF\n\n## Employment Type\n\nFull time\n\n## Department\n\nAgency\n\n📍 USA & Canada. Remote or in-person SF.\n\n⏰ Working hours are **PST**\n\n## About Valid\n\nFounded in July 2023, Valid is a seed-stage company operating at Series A scale, headquartered in San Francisco.\n\nIn under two years, we’ve grown from 5 people to 40+, deployed over $1B in ad spend, and built a full-stack, tech-enabled advertising company serving enterprise consumer customers.\n\nWe’re well-capitalized and backed by top Silicon Valley investors including Canaan, Neo, and others.\n\n## The Role\n\n- A customer obsessed marketing strategist\n\n- First in line to try the newest AI marketing tools\n\n- Passionate about ad networks and performance marketing strategy\n\n- Obsessed with discovering and tracking social media trends\n\n- Customer obsessed (we put it in their twice on purpose!)\n\n\n_We believe that the best form of marketing is AI-assisted, data-driven and human in-the-loop. This role is for an analyst who can interface with the client to help set and execute user acquisition strategies._\n\n## Responsibilities\n\n- Own performance marketing account management for app clients.\n\n- Execute media planning confidently across paid social (Meta, TikTok, Snapchat) and paid search (ASA, Google UAC) channels.\n\n- Orchestrate creative production and manage the end-to-end flow until assets are launched in ad accounts.\n\n- Own, ideate, and iterate on creative testing frameworks tailored to each app’s context.\n\n- Engage in internal & external communication to collaborate with cross-functional teams and present campaign reports to stakeholders and clients.\n\n- Analyze campaign data using strong analytical skills and derive actionable insights to improve performance.\n\n- Contribute to growth marketing discussions on LTV/CAC, payback periods, MRR/ARR, run rates, and more.\n\n- Use MMPs and analytics dashboards for reporting, and collaborate with the Valid product team on data management best practices.\n\n- Conduct A/B & multivariate testing to improve performance and generate insights.\n\n\n## Required Qualifications\n\n- 2–3 years of growth marketing or user acquisition experience\n\n- 1–2 years of app performance marketing experience, primarily paid social UA (this will be tested)\n\n- Hands-on experience with MMPs like AppsFlyer, Adjust, Singular, Branch, Kochava, or AirBridge\n\n- Proficient in iOS app attribution and well-versed in SKAdNetwork, ATT, and probabilistic attribution (this will be tested)\n\n- Strong familiarity with paid media campaigns specific to apps: Meta AEM, TikTok ADC, Google UAC\n\n- Track record of managing iOS app campaigns that optimize for CPA, ROAS, and LTV\n\n- Able to multitask and prioritize effectively in a fast-paced environment\n\n\n## Preferred Qualifications\n\n- Industry Expertise: Actively learns and shares new industry insights\n\n- Experience with consumer subscription apps\n\n- Freemium model familiarity for subscription apps\n\n- Understanding of user onboarding flows and paywall testing\n\n- Adaptability to platform changes, including iOS and social media algorithms\n\n\n## What You’ll Be Getting\n\n- Work on a global team with flexibility and a collaborative startup culture\n\n- Annual company offsite - we gather in a new location each year to connect and celebrate\n\n\n## Compensation Range\n\n- Competitive salary based on experience and location\n\n- Benefits: 401k, healthcare, FSA, lunch (for in-person days)\n\n- Location: Remote friendly in USA or Canada with a preference for in-person out of our office in San Francisco.\n\n\n[Apply for this Job](https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/Valid/b712b932-41ba-4503-9c79-7b0e8605cda8/application)",
